        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The last arg for vim.notify is nil. Can it be an object like `{ source = \"mini.snippets\", text = \"No matches in context\", lang = \"\" }` for filtering?\n\nI though about supplying at least `source` in all notifications across all modules, but that seems unnecessary. All messages contain module's name in parenthesis as prefix, so doing `vim.startswith(msg, '(mini.snippets)')` is equivalent to potential `opts.source == 'mini.snippets'` . Similar for actual message text. Supplying full context to notification seems also redundant.",
